-          "quote": "Fix a finite dimension $d\\ge1$ and a discrete filtered probability space $(\\Omega,\\mathcal F,(\\mathcal F_k)_{k\\ge0},P)$ as in [[def-filtration-and-filtered-probability-space]]. A sequence $x_k:\\Omega\\to\\mathbb R^d$ is an iterate process when each coordinate is $\\mathcal F_k$-measurable; a sequence $G_k:\\Omega\\to\\mathbb R^d$ is an oracle process when each coordinate is $\\mathcal F_{k+1}$-measurable. These are coordinatewise instances of [[def-random-element-and-real-random-variable]] and [[def-adapted-and-integrable-stochastic-process]]. Assume the coordinates used in a conditional moment are square-integrable.\n\nFor deterministic stepsizes $\\alpha_k>0$, the unconstrained Robbins–Monro/SGD update is\n$$x_{k+1}=x_k-\\alpha_kG_k.$$\nFor a differentiable objective $f:\\mathbb R^d\\to\\mathbb R$, the oracle is conditionally unbiased when $\\mathbb E[G_k\\mid\\mathcal F_k]=\\nabla f(x_k)$ coordinatewise almost surely; it has conditional bias $b_k$ when $\\mathbb E[G_k\\mid\\mathcal F_k]=\\nabla f(x_k)+b_k$. The conditional variance of a vector is the sum of the scalar conditional variances of its coordinates, using [[def-conditional-variance]]. By [[lem-conditional-variance-is-well-defined-and-has-the-second-moment-formula]], it satisfies\n$$\\mathbb E[\\|G_k\\|_2^2\\mid\\mathcal F_k]=\\|\\mathbb E[G_k\\mid\\mathcal F_k]\\|_2^2+\\operatorname{Var}(G_k\\mid\\mathcal F_k)$$\nalmost surely. All conditional expectations are coordinatewise instances of [[def-conditional-expectation-as-an-ae-class]], whose existence assumes the [[def-axiom-of-choice]]. No independence across iterations is part of this definition.\n\nThe conditional second-moment bound $\\mathbb E[\\|G_k\\|_2^2\\mid\\mathcal F_k]\\le M_k^2$ and the conditional variance bound $\\operatorname{Var}(G_k\\mid\\mathcal F_k)\\le\\sigma_k^2$ are distinct hypotheses; the latter combines with conditional unbiasedness through the displayed identity.",
